<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Annotations by Pablo Caro - nix</title><link>/en/</link><description>Anotaciones</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><item><title>qemu-wasm: full virtual machines inside your browser</title><link>/en/qemu-wasm-maquinas-virtuales-en-el-navegador</link><description>&lt;p&gt;qemu-wasm ports QEMU to WebAssembly to boot a full x86_64 virtual machine inside the browser. trynix.dev runs any nixpkgs package from the last 13 years, and a GitHub Action boots a PR's build from a single link.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-09-11:/en/qemu-wasm-maquinas-virtuales-en-el-navegador</guid><category>Tools</category><category>webassembly</category><category>qemu</category><category>browser</category><category>nix</category><category>virtual-machines</category><category>github-actions</category></item></channel></rss>